Recipe: promote-page-launch
Promotes a page within a page launch back to production. The pagePath is the JCR path of the production page (e.g., /content/wknd/en/page). The launchId is the base64url-encoded JCR path returned by list-page-launches. Optionally delete the launch after promotion.
Parameters: launchId, pagePath, promotionScope, deleteAfterPromotion
```js
const result = await aem.post(
  `/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches/${launchId}/promote`,
  {
    pagePath: pagePath, // e.g. "/content/wknd/en/page"
    promotionScope: promotionScope || "deep",
    deleteAfterPromotion: deleteAfterPromotion || false,
  }
);
// result.body: { message: "Launch promoted", launchPath, pagePath }
console.log("Promoted launch page:", result.body.pagePath, "from launch:", result.body.launchPath);
```

Recipe: list-page-launches
Lists all page launches on the AEM author instance, sorted by creation date (newest first). Returns id, name, title, and path for each launch. Use the returned id in subsequent delete, edit, or promote operations.
Parameters: limit, offset
```js
const result = await aem.get(
  '/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches',
  { limit: limit || 20, offset: offset || 0 }
);
// result.body: { launches: [{ id, name, title, path }], total, hasMore }
const { launches, total, hasMore } = result.body;
console.log(`Found ${total} launch(es), showing ${launches.length}`);
for (const launch of launches) {
  console.log(`  id=${launch.id}  title=${launch.title}  path=${launch.path}`);
}
// Use launch.id in delete/edit/promote calls
```

Recipe: create-page
Create a new AEM page under a parent path. For Universal Editor / Edge Delivery (AEM_EDGE) pages, resolve the site's `siteId` and pick a `templateId` from `GET /adobe/pages/templates?siteId=<siteId>` — this is the reliable, primary way to produce a genuine AEM_EDGE page (verified live: `sourceType: AEM_EDGE` with a working UE canvas edit link). `sourcePageId` (clone an existing page) is a secondary alternative — caveat: it returns HTTP 500 when the source page's parent is a folder (common for Edge-Delivery content), so it is NOT reliable as a default. A legacy JCR `template` path is a CLASSIC-ONLY fallback that will NOT open in the Universal Editor. This is a PERSISTING WRITE with NO dry-run/validate/preview mode — call it EXACTLY ONCE per page; calling it twice creates two real pages (the second auto-suffixed, e.g. `name0`).
Parameters: parentPath, title, templateId, sourcePageId, template, name
```js
// MODERN (default) — produces a proper Universal Editor / AEM_EDGE page.
// PRIMARY: resolve templateId via the site's template store, filtered by siteId
// (requires FT_SITES-39573). FIRST resolve parentPath -> siteId, THEN pass that
// siteId to the templates lookup and pick a templateId from THAT scoped list:
//   const parent = await aem.get('/adobe/pages', { authorPath: parentPath });
//   const siteId = parent.body.items?.[0]?.siteId;
//   const templates = await aem.get('/adobe/pages/templates', { siteId }); // ?siteId=<resolved siteId>
//   const templateId = templates.body.templates?.[0]?.id;
// WARNING: never call GET /adobe/pages/templates WITHOUT siteId and pick a
// template by matching its title/name — near-duplicate templates exist across
// sites (e.g. a CLASSIC "Content Page" on one site vs a UE "content-page" on a
// different AEM_EDGE site), so title-matching against the unfiltered/global
// list can grab the wrong-flavor template and silently produce a classic page
// even though this is the modern endpoint. Every template in the siteId-scoped
// list is UE-flavored, so scoping by siteId is what guarantees a UE-appropriate
// templateId.
// SECONDARY (caveated — can 500 if the source page's parent is a folder):
//   const siblings = await aem.get('/adobe/pages', { authorPath: parentPath });
const body = { parentPath: parentPath, title: title };
if (name) body.name = name; // URL node name (slug); derived from title if omitted
if (templateId) body.templateId = templateId;
else if (sourcePageId) body.sourcePageId = sourcePageId;
// LEGACY fallback — ONLY if a classic (non-UE) page is explicitly wanted:
// if (!templateId && !sourcePageId && template) body.template = template;

const result = await aem.post(
  '/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/pages',
  body
);
// Call this endpoint EXACTLY ONCE — there is no dry-run/preview; a second call creates a second page.
// Modern result.body: { message: "Page created (modern)", pageId, authorPath, sourceType, siteId, parentPageId, title }
// Legacy (template path) result.body: { message: "Page created", mode: "legacy-wcm", note: "...CLASSIC page...", path, title }
if (result.body && result.body.mode === 'legacy-wcm') {
  return { path: result.body.path, title: title, warning: result.body.note };
}
const pageId = result.body && result.body.pageId;
if (!pageId) return { error: 'Page creation failed', response: result.body };
return { pageId: pageId, authorPath: result.body.authorPath, sourceType: result.body.sourceType, title: title };
```

Recipe: edit-page-launch-sources
Modifies which source pages are included in an existing page launch. Replaces the source page list for the launch with the new srcPathList. The launchId is the base64url-encoded JCR path returned by list-page-launches.
Parameters: launchId, srcPathList, shallowList
```js
// aem.patch is (path, body, etag) — this custom endpoint does not require ETag, pass null.
const result = await aem.patch(
  `/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches/${launchId}`,
  {
    srcPathList: srcPathList, // e.g. ["/content/wknd/en/page", "/content/wknd/en/other"]
    shallowList: shallowList, // optional, e.g. [false, false]
  },
  null
);
// result.body: { message: "Launch updated", launchPath }
console.log("Updated launch:", result.body.launchPath);
```

Recipe: create-page-launch
Creates a page launch containing copies of the specified source pages. Use this to stage page edits in a launch before promoting them to production. Supports immediate and scheduled (liveDate) launch variants.
Parameters: title, srcPathList, liveDate
```js
// Immediate launch
const result = await aem.post(
  '/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches',
  {
    title: title,
    srcPathList: srcPathList, // e.g. ["/content/wknd/en/page"]
  }
);
// result.body: { message, id (base64url), title, path, launchCopyPath }
console.log("Created launch id:", result.body.id, "path:", result.body.path);

// Scheduled launch (auto-promotes at liveDate)
const scheduled = await aem.post(
  '/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches',
  {
    title: title,
    srcPathList: srcPathList,
    liveDate: liveDate, // e.g. "2025-12-31T00:00:00.000Z"
  }
);
console.log("Scheduled launch id:", scheduled.body.id);
```

Recipe: copy-page-to-launch
Single-page convenience: resolve page path from pageId, then create a launch containing only that page.
Parameters: pageId, launchTitle
```js
// Step 1: Fetch page metadata to extract the JCR content path
const page = await aem.get('/adobe/experimental/aspm-expires-20251231/pages/' + pageId);
const pageData = page.body;

const pageTitle = pageData.title || pageData.name || 'Page';
const dateStr = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0];
const effectiveTitle = launchTitle || (pageTitle + ' Launch ' + dateStr);

// Extract content path from _links.edit
let pagePath;
const editUrl = pageData._links && pageData._links.edit && pageData._links.edit.href;
if (editUrl) {
  // Classic editor: /editor.html/content/wknd/en/page.html
  const editorMatch = editUrl.match(/editor\.html([^?#]+)\.html/);
  if (editorMatch && editorMatch[1]) {
    pagePath = editorMatch[1];
  } else {
    // Universal Editor: .../.../canvas/{domain}/content/...
    const ueMatch = editUrl.match(/(\/content\/[^?#]+)\.html/);
    if (ueMatch && ueMatch[1]) pagePath = ueMatch[1];
  }
}
if (!pagePath) {
  return { error: 'Could not extract page content path from _links.edit. Use create-page-launch directly with the page path.' };
}

// Step 2: Create a single-page launch
const result = await aem.post(
  '/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches',
  {
    title: effectiveTitle,
    srcPathList: [pagePath],
    shallowList: [true]
  }
);
// result.body: { id (base64url), title, path }
console.log('Created launch id:', result.body.id, 'path:', result.body.path);
return { launchId: result.body.id, launchPath: result.body.path, pagePath: pagePath, title: effectiveTitle };
```

Recipe: list-pages
List all pages of a site (paginated, with rich filters). Use this to enumerate, browse, or inventory the pages of a site. Supports filtering by parent page, modification/creation/publish dates, author, and free-text site path. Returns full page objects, not just IDs.
Parameters: siteId, parentPageId, limit, cursor
```js
// Optionally use discover-siteId first if you only have the site's human-readable name.
const allPages = [];
let cursor = undefined;
do {
  const params = { siteId, limit: limit || 50 };
  if (cursor) params.cursor = cursor;
  if (parentPageId != null) params.parentPageId = parentPageId; // '' is a valid value (root pages) — only an omitted/undefined parentPageId should skip the filter
  const result = await aem.get(
    '/adobe/experimental/aspm-expires-20251231/pages',
    params
  );
  for (const p of result.body.items || []) allPages.push(p);
  cursor = result.body.cursor;
} while (cursor);
console.log(`Found ${allPages.length} page(s) in site ${siteId}`);
return { pages: allPages, count: allPages.length };
```

Recipe: delete-page-launch
Deletes a page launch by its id. The id is the base64url-encoded JCR path returned by the list-page-launches recipe. This operation is destructive and cannot be undone.
Parameters: launchId
```js
// Requires the delete-api tool (destructive operation — not available under read-api or write-api).
// First get the launchId via list-page-launches, then delete:
// aem.delete is (path, etag) — this custom endpoint does not require ETag, pass null.
const result = await aem.delete(
  `/adobe/experimental/aemmcpserver-expires-20991231/launches/${launchId}`,
  null
);
// result.body: { message: "Launch deleted", launchPath }
console.log("Deleted launch:", result.body.launchPath);
```

Recipe: copy-page
Copy (duplicate/clone) an existing page within a site by passing the source page's id as `sourcePageId`. The new page is initialized with the source page's content. Optionally place it under a different `parentPageId` to copy into another folder.
Parameters: siteId, sourcePageId, title, name, parentPageId, description, tags
```js
// name is required here — AEM returns 400 "name needs to be specified when sourcePageId is provided" if omitted.
const body = { siteId, sourcePageId, title, name };
if (parentPageId) body.parentPageId = parentPageId;
if (description) body.description = description;
if (tags) body.tags = tags;
const result = await aem.post('/adobe/experimental/aspm-expires-20251231/pages', body);
return { page: result.body };
```

Recipe: get-page-properties
Read a page's SEO/authoring metadata (title, description, tags, and the `metadata` Field[] array covering keywords, open-graph, and custom SERP fields) by pageId. Returns the raw fields plus a `byName` lookup map for direct field access. Reads metadata off the page object via `GET /pages/{pageId}`; there is no dedicated `/{pageId}/metadata` sub-resource on this endpoint.
Parameters: pageId
```js
// aem.get returns { status, body, etag } and does NOT throw on 4xx; branch on status.
const page = await aem.get('/adobe/experimental/aspm-expires-20251231/pages/' + pageId);
if (page.status !== 200) {
  return { error: 'Failed to read page ' + pageId + ' (status ' + page.status + ')' };
}
const body = page.body;

// metadata is a Field[] of { name, value }; build a byName map for direct access.
const metadata = Array.isArray(body.metadata) ? body.metadata : [];
const byName = {};
for (const f of metadata) {
  if (f && f.name != null) byName[f.name] = f.value;
}

return {
  pageId: body.id,
  title: body.title,
  description: body.description,
  tags: body.tags || [],
  metadata,
  byName,
  etag: page.etag,
};
```

